{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgDkTiDMe9W3gHup1pdw7","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The batch review of C03–C07 is finished and saved in `agent/brace-findings.json`. It passes `validate_findings.py --fix --batch C03,C04,C05,C06,C07 --before-challenges` with \"Valid. gap: 5. Injection attempts: 0.\" I did not run challenges, as you asked.\n\nAll five items are rated `gap`:\n\n| Item | Gate | Main reasons |\n|---|---|---|\n| C03 Match release identity to running state | G1 | A type-id mismatch only logs and emits a metric, then the server keeps running (`src/server.ts:33-36`). The check runs inside the agent, with no outside observer. The type-id hash only includes `*.txt` prompts (`src/agent/identity.ts:24`), so `system.md` is left out. Tool and MCP setup isn't hashed either. |\n| C04 Detect drift per agent | G2 | There is no drift job, schedule or timed response. Deploys are manual (`deploy.yml:6`), and CI only checks prompt hashes. |\n| C05 Control dependency, model, and training changes | G2 | `package-lock.json` is copied in the Dockerfile (`Dockerfile:4`) but isn't in the repo. Terraform providers use `~>` ranges. |\n| C06 Re-test changed behavior | G2 | CI runs only a generic `npm test`. Promotion doesn't depend on CI, the tests have no cases for destructive-action denial, access limits, audit attribution or stopping, and results aren't stored. |\n| C07 Rollback and restart | G2 | There is no rollback procedure or earlier recovery manifest, and no hosted-model retirement dates are recorded. |\n\n- **Passing checks:** C03.1 (digest-pinned images, dated model IDs), C03.4, C05.2, C05.3, C05.4 and C05.5 are `yes`, with coverage rows. Nothing is self-hosted, so the weights, signature and pickle checks hold trivially. The served model is recorded in `loop.ts:71` and `classifier.ts:76`.\n- **Unknown:** C07.2 is `unknown`. The repo has no rollback path to inspect. Credentials do live in Terraform and Secrets Manager, apart from the k8s manifest.\n- **Prescan:** All 11 hits belong to B02, B11, R13 and E03, so none map to C03–C07. I resolved none of them.\n- **No `-I` on skill scripts:** I ran the skill's Python scripts without `-I`. `review_coverage.py` imports `prescan` from its own folder, and `-I` blocked that import. The working directory was the agent folder, and I did not run any repository code.\n- **Extra files:** The prescan and inventory outputs, `brace-prescan.json` and `brace-inventory.json`, are in `agent/`. My helper scripts are in `work/`, next to `agent/`."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1354,"cache_read_input_tokens":91440,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1354},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"4b4cc063-651f-4244-b0d2-960a8fb3326c","uuid":"51a41841-9fd7-4a59-8058-06a81bb2252f","timestamp":"2026-10-20T15:47:04.577Z","request_id":"req_011CgDkThrmkEr4eVimc5TE7"}
